oved, and several temporary files including a private key were left in /tmp — unnecessary retained residue from the verification step rather than the task's core deliverable.\",\"limitations\":[\"The client-side verification key added to root's authorized_keys (cmd-5f0d05a1fc884576) was not shown to be removed at any point in the trace, so it may still grant passwordless root access on node1.\",\"Temporary files including a private key (/tmp/client_ed25519) remain in /tmp per the after_executor snapshot and were not cleaned up.\",\"No evidence was captured of failure/error conditions for a client that does NOT trust the CA (e.g., confirming the negative case of pinning-free rejection), though this was not strictly required by the task wording.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"ca-created","requirement":"Create an SSH certificate authority on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"An ED25519 CA keypair was generated at /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_ca_key with fingerprint SHA256:IXSC9lpHS.../H/Q, private key mode 600, public key mode 644.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2d51ffc292834d81"]},{"id":"host-cert-signed-served","requirement":"Host presents a certificate signed by the CA","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node1 ed25519 host public key was signed by the CA with principals node1 and 10.100.239.10, installed as /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub, and sshd_config/sshd -T confirm the HostCertificate directive is active and loaded (after an SELinux relabel fix).","evidence_ids":["cmd-b290cedbf7344888","cmd-351c1d22b27945b9","cmd-212448f718d1415a","cmd-a35c590efdb64a98"]},{"id":"client-connects-without-pinning","requirement":"A client trusting only the CA (no host-key pinning) connects successfully","status":"satisfied","summary":"A client known_hosts file containing only an @cert-authority entry (no pinned host key) with StrictHostKeyChecking=yes successfully validated the host via 'Host is known and matches the ED25519-CERT host certificate' and executed a command, 